\subsection{Check if we need to log in to LADOK}

There are two cases:
\begin{enumerate}
\item We get a 401 unauthorized from a LADOK host in \emph{our} environment.
\item We get redirected to the login server.
\end{enumerate}
Thus, we can detect this with either the return code or if the URL starts with
the URL to the login service, then we need to log in.
However, as noted above, this only applies if we're not already underway with a
login.

The restriction to our own environment in the first case deserves an
explanation.
Thanks to [[add_handler]], one [[AutologinSession]] can be shared by several
modules, and in particular a production handler and a test-environment handler
can serve the same session---that way they share the SSO and MFA state, so the
user authenticates only once for both environments.
But [[login]] can only establish a session for its own [[self.__base_url]]: if
we claimed a 401 from the \emph{other} environment, we would log in to the
wrong host and either hand back an unrelated page as the response or loop,
re-issuing a request we can never fix.
An earlier version checked [[if "ladok.se" in response.url]], which matched
both environments---and, since it searched the whole URL rather than the host,
even a 401 from [[evil.com/ladok.se]] would have triggered a login.
<<check if we're redirected to login server>>=
if response.status_code == requests.codes.unauthorized \
     and self.same_environment(response.url):
  logger.debug(
    "SSOlogin detected %s for %s",
    response.status_code,
    weblogin._sanitize_url(response.url),
  )
  return True
elif response.url.startswith(self.__login_url):
  logger.debug(
    "SSOlogin detected login redirect %s",
    weblogin._sanitize_url(response.url),
  )
  return True

return False
@

\subsection{Which environment does a URL belong to?}

We cannot simply compare the URL's host to [[self.__base_url]]'s host:
LADOK serves its API from [[www.start.ladok.se]] and [[www.test.ladok.se]],
while the login redirects use [[start.ladok.se]] and [[start.test.ladok.se]].
Exact host equality would thus miss the very 401s that need a login.
What reliably separates the two environments is the domain: every test host
lives under [[test.ladok.se]], no production host does.
So we compare \emph{environment membership}: the URL's host must be a
[[ladok.se]] host, and it must be a test host exactly when our own base URL
is.
We parse with [[urllib.parse]] rather than substring matching so that only
the host---not the path or query---can make the decision.
<<SSOlogin methods>>=
def same_environment(self, url):
  """
  Returns True if `url` refers to a LADOK host in the same environment
  (production or test) as this handler, False otherwise.
  """
  host = urllib.parse.urlparse(url, allow_fragments=False).netloc
  if host != "ladok.se" and not host.endswith(".ladok.se"):
    return False
  own_host = urllib.parse.urlparse(self.__base_url).netloc
  return self.is_test_environment_host(host) \
      == self.is_test_environment_host(own_host)

@staticmethod
def is_test_environment_host(host):
  """
  Returns True if the domain name `host` belongs to LADOK's test
  environment, False for any other host (including production ones).
  """
  return host == "test.ladok.se" or host.endswith(".test.ladok.se")
@

Let's verify that each handler claims exactly the 401s of its own
environment: the production handler must claim production API hosts but
ignore the test environment, and vice versa.
We also check that a [[ladok.se]] appearing in the \emph{path} of a URL on
some other host no longer fools the check.
<<test functions>>=
def make_unauthorized_response(url):
  response = requests.Response()
  response.status_code = requests.codes.unauthorized
  response.url = url
  response.history = []
  return response

def test_need_login_claims_own_environment():
  prod = ladok.SSOlogin("KTH Royal Institute of Technology")
  test = ladok.SSOlogin("KTH Royal Institute of Technology",
                        test_environment=True)

  prod_401 = make_unauthorized_response(
    "https://www.start.ladok.se/gui/proxy/resultat")
  assert prod.need_login(prod_401)
  assert not test.need_login(prod_401)

def test_need_login_ignores_other_environment():
  prod = ladok.SSOlogin("KTH Royal Institute of Technology")
  test = ladok.SSOlogin("KTH Royal Institute of Technology",
                        test_environment=True)

  test_401 = make_unauthorized_response(
    "https://www.test.ladok.se/gui/proxy/resultat")
  assert not prod.need_login(test_401)
  assert test.need_login(test_401)

def test_need_login_ignores_ladok_in_path():
  prod = ladok.SSOlogin("KTH Royal Institute of Technology")

  lookalike_401 = make_unauthorized_response(
    "https://evil.com/ladok.se/gui/proxy/resultat")
  assert not prod.need_login(lookalike_401)
@

